MK1 is a rewrite of the original assembly language for [ok], which was called [MK2].

[ok]: https://github.com/htogta/ok
[MK2]: https://github.com/htogta/MK2

The idea behind MK1 is to be easier to implement/bootstrap, while adding some support that [MK2] previously lacked.

To read more about the language itself, see the [OVERVIEW].

For a rough outline of the grammar in EBNF, see [GRAMMAR].

